<title>BELGIUM: Belgian car registrations down 13.3% in March.</title>
<headline>Belgian car registrations down 13.3% in March.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian new car registrations fell 13.3 percent in March compared with the same year ago period, according to figures released on Wednesday by the Belgian Automobile Manufacturers Federation, FEBIAC.</p>
<p>Registrations were down 7.3 percent in the year to March.</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CAR REGISTRATIONS March 97	March 96</p>
<p>    Month			   39,329	  45,352</p>
<p>    Cumulative Jan-March     122,918	 132,621</p>
<p>March registrations by manufacturer and market share for those above three percent versus 1996 period.</p>
<p> VW	 9,064 (23.0 pct)  vs   9,041 (19.9 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot  6,208 (15.8 pct)  vs   6,264 (13.8 pct)</p>
<p> Ford</p>
<p>   Motor  4,157 (10.6 pct)  vs   5,922 (13.1 pct)</p>
<p> GM	 3,964 (10.1 pct)  vs   4,404 ( 9.7 pct)</p>
<p> Renault  2,861 ( 7.3 pct)  vs   4,983 (11.0 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota   2,023 ( 5.1 pct)  vs   2,069 ( 4.6 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat     1,888 ( 4.8 pct)  vs   2,224 ( 4.9 pct)</p>
<p> BMW	1,697 ( 4.3 pct)  vs   1,872 ( 4.1 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan   1,422 ( 3.6 pct)  vs   1,072 ( 2.4 pct)</p>
<p> Mercedes 1,192 ( 3.0 pct)  vs   1,168 ( 2.6 pct)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
